{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01EGs5FRSJtxAgn4Z4WcPQkK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014GFpmA4PXxB5xgp6CKc4V2","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nMulti-stream Round 0: parallelize AIR processing across CUDA streams\n\nProcess Round 0 AIRs across 4 OS threads, each with its own CUDA\nstream (cudaStreamPerThread), enabling concurrent GPU kernel execution\non idle SMs. This dramatically improves Round 0 performance when there\nare many small AIRs (APC 100/300).\n\nKey changes:\n- Add MemCopyD2HStreamSync trait with to_host_on_current_stream() that\n  uses per-thread stream sync instead of global COPY_EVENT mutex\n- Extract per-AIR Round 0 work into standalone process_air_round0()\n- Restructure loop into 3 phases: build work items, parallel process,\n  scatter results\n- Sort AIRs by descending height for load balance\n- Threshold: only multi-thread when >= 100 AIRs (avoids regression\n  with few large AIRs that already saturate the GPU)\n\nResults at APC 300: Round 0 669ms -> 351ms (1.91x), STARK excl trace\n2282ms -> 1969ms (1.16x). No regression at APC 0.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\n)\"","description":"Commit implementation changes"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":145,"cache_read_input_tokens":121555,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":145},"output_tokens":48,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"60c64baa-adc7-41a6-a4e9-76f47ba81313","uuid":"1dfd6283-e076-46c4-918c-a13a78a4f2d9"}
